<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.1.13.2.1"/>
    <code code="10154-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Chief complaint Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Wheeze and tight chest for three days with a cold, a week after returning from abroad. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Miss Wheatley returned from abroad eight days ago. She was well all summer: she used her reliever only two or three times a month, never needed the standby prednisone, and feels the time away did her good. Five days ago, in the first cold, damp days after her return, she caught a cold with a sore throat and runny nose. For three days her chest has been tight and wheezy; she woke twice last night and has used six to eight extra inhalations of budesonide-formoterol on each of the last two days, as her action plan allows. This morning her peak flow was 280 L/min, in the yellow zone, and she called the clinic. She can speak in full sentences and has no chest pain or green sputum. She has been very busy since her return and is anxious not to lose time. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Cold five days ago; asthma worse for three days</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Woke twice last night; six to eight reliever inhalations a day; peak flow 280 L/min this morning</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>As-needed budesonide-formoterol (GINA track 1, step 2); yellow zone of her action plan</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Sore throat and runny nose; temperature 37.6 °C; no chest pain or purulent sputum</td></tr><tr><td>Risk history</td><td>No previous exacerbation needing oral corticosteroids, emergency care or admission</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

