    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1773-09-21; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Alert, sitting upright, speaking in full sentences; no accessory muscle use</td></tr><tr><td>Vital signs</td><td>Pulse 98, respiratory rate 20, oxygen saturation 96 percent on room air, temperature 37.6 °C; peak flow 270 L/min (68 percent of her best)</td></tr><tr><td>Head, eyes, ears, nose, and throat</td><td>Red throat without exudate; clear nasal discharge; no sinus tenderness</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Scattered expiratory wheeze with good air entry; no crackles</td></tr><tr><td>Reassessment after 30 minutes</td><td>After two inhalations of budesonide-formoterol with a spacer: peak flow 330 L/min (82 percent), wheeze much reduced, pulse 90, respiratory rate 16</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

